From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:14:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] activation: The desktop and the session's layer-shell windows
 keep the active output

Workspace::setActiveWindow() moved the active output to the output of every
window it activated. At the start of a session the shell puts up surfaces on
every screen, in the order its screens come in, and each takes the focus as it
maps: Plasma maps one desktop window per output, the first activated because no
window is active, and ksplashqml maps an overlay layer-shell window with the
exclusive keyboard on every screen, each activated in turn. The last one left the
active output on the screen it served last, not on the screen marked main in
Display Settings where the session starts, so the windows mapped next, the KDE
Wallet prompt or an autostart program, opened there until the pointer moved.

The desktop and the layer-shell windows are not where the person works: their
activation no longer moves the active output. The pointer, a click, switching to an
output and the activation of a program's own window move it as before; a launcher
opens on the active output, so activating it moves nothing.

A trace of Workspace::setActiveOutput() in a session of three outputs named the
path for both: addWaylandWindow, activateWindow, requestFocus, setActiveWindow,
setActiveOutput. KWin master and Plasma/6.7 still have it (bugs.kde.org 500904,
501527, 489904).

